# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Everything a user generates. None of it belongs on GitHub.
#
#  Your agenda contains your courses, your grades, your deadlines and your
#  mail. Treat this file as a safety rail, not a suggestion: if you add a new
#  output path anywhere in the pipeline, add it here in the same commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The working directory. Every scrape, render, plan and ledger lands here.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# Your answers to onboarding: timezone, school, courses, difficulty, schedule.
config.json
config.json.bak

# Environment overrides for .mcp.json (${VAR} interpolation).
.env

# Rendered pages.
agenda.html
agenda-preview.html
demo-agenda.html

# Rotating local state mirrors written by drive-bundle.mjs --pack.
backups/

# Any base64 envelope written anywhere (payload, mirror, oversize spill).
*.b64.txt

# Credentials, in every shape anything in this repo has ever used.
*credentials*.json
*.dpapi
.d2l-session/

# Python virtualenvs for the optional Gradescope extra.
.venv*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node.
node_modules/

# Editor and OS noise.
*.bak
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Screenshots. Nothing in the pipeline writes an image, so a blanket *.png ignore
# only ever blocked the one image this project wants committed - the README
# screenshot. Ignore the two places a stray one actually lands (the repo root,
# where you drop a screengrab while debugging, and data/, already covered above)
# and leave docs/images/ committable.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
